From bbd9534563e848921b9357897e6e5234fb9a7b69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <gab@chx-labs.org>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:52:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] [Bugfix][V2] Resolve deferred mamba state copies by
 request slot

Under pipeline parallelism the sampled outputs of step T are consumed by
step T + pp_size, so the mamba align postprocess runs for a batch whose
rows are no longer the ones the gathered block tables describe: it indexed
the persistent input_block_tables by batch row with a stale idx_mapping,
copying recurrent state through other requests' freed or reallocated block
ids (silent NaN corruption, or an illegal memory access where the read
lands unmapped).

Capture the request-indexed block tables for the state copies and index
their rows by request slot. Those tables are staged per request and only
grow while a request lives, and freed slots are already filtered out of the
deferred idx_mapping, so the copy resolves the same block ids it would have
seen at its own step. Everything else keeps using the batch-ordered gather.
